		// Verbatim replay of the retail create POST-world-entry in-world server burst, exactly as captured in
		// the retail create capture (Captures/account-stricken997-character-Strie-create.json, GameServer port
		// 7029). After the one-shot world-entry download (rows 65-114) retail does NOT go silent: it answers the
		// client's 0x02165EFF request ids (0x000818A2-0x000818A6) with small 0x2000 acknowledgements and streams
		// an in-world burst (0x96B8DC59 / 0x642CD3D6 / 0xF98E10B3) before the client finally sends
		// ReadyForPlayScreen (row 203). Our server previously sent none of this, so the new character flooded
		// unanswered 0x02165EFF and the client hung on the loading screen, never reaching ReadyForPlayScreen.
		//
		// These are the server->client (DL) packets from capture rows 116-130 (acks of the first 0x02165EFF
		// batch), 149-174 (the in-world 0x96B8DC59/0x642CD3D6/0xF98E10B3 burst) and 197-201 (acks of the second
		// 0x02165EFF batch). They are replayed byte-for-byte. The create flow deliberately reuses the retail
		// temporary client instance 0x02165EFF, ack 0xC350 and the static request ids 0x000818A2-0x000818A6, so a
		// verbatim replay reproduces the retail conversation exactly. Pong/LatencyCheckResponse (rows 115/202)
		// are intentionally excluded - those are produced by the normal Ping/LatencyCheck handlers.

